-- The rules `verify-unfold-imports.l4` imports. Nothing here is contradictory.
--
-- Neither rule says GIVETH, on purpose: its return type is INFERRED, so the
-- annotation carries an inference variable that only this module's own
-- substitution resolves. `l4 verify` must zonk an imported body before it can
-- see that the rule returns a BOOLEAN; without that, neither rule is unfolded
-- and the importer's contradiction is missed (measured 2026-09-29).

DECLARE Facts HAS
    `the act was accidental` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the act was lawful`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `harm was caused`        IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN f IS A Facts
DECIDE `the exception applies` f IF
        f's `the act was accidental`
    AND f's `the act was lawful`

-- A guarded chain, so the ladder must also know this body is boolean to draw it
-- as structure rather than a leaf.
GIVEN f IS A Facts
DECIDE `the offence is made out` f IF
    IF `the exception applies` f
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE f's `harm was caused`
